1
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:12,960
Brighten up the peace,
then try stepping away.

2
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:28,800
about the rainy aftermath when
it feels like someone is calling.

3
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:32,660
I walked while looking back.

4
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:35,320
Holding hands with Gā-chan,

5
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:42,280
that strange feeling I had back then.

6
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:47,740
So the tiles on the arcade street

7
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:53,520
I walked only on the black ones.

8
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,680
Everyone was a child once,

9
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:01,840
but everyone has forgotten.

10
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:09,120
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

11
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:14,700
Try turning that corner.

12
00:01:15,740 --> 00:01:19,900
You can meet everyone, everyone.

13
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:27,840
There are turtles over there
surely there are turtles.

14
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:33,020
Everyone, come to our town!

15
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:34,600
Thank you.

16
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:39,800
The departure of Yone and the onigiri.

17
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:48,200
Please, someone, help me!

18
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:50,246
Reiko,

19
00:01:50,296 --> 00:01:54,140
Reiko, please, anything to eat.

20
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:55,520
No way.

21
00:01:56,240 --> 00:02:01,800
Reeeko!
At this rate, I might starve to death!

22
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,900
This is for your own good, Ryo-chan.

23
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:06,620
You meanie, Reiko! You swan-hearted coward!

24
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:09,840
No matter what you say, no means no.

25
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:15,300
Nakagawa-kun.

26
00:02:16,820 --> 00:02:19,980
Stop it, senpai! Don't come any closer!

27
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:26,520
Nakagawa, forget the 100 yen. Even 50 or 30 yen will do,
just spare some for me.

28
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:30,780
Sorry, senpai,
but I can't lend you any money.

29
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:34,900
You know this too, senpai.
It's the Chief's orders.

30
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:37,560
Nakagawa, nobody would find out
if you just kept quiet, you know.

31
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:40,720
Normally, after getting burned once,
a person would learn their lesson,

32
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:45,020
but Ryo-chan, you keep going broke every
month and still haven't learned, have you?

33
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:50,120
Everyone knows Edo folk never carry spare change,
it's the rule.

34
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:54,480
Then, true to your Edo spirit,
go hungry with dignity and stop complaining.

35
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:55,520
Chief.

36
00:02:56,320 --> 00:03:01,960
You spent your whole paycheck on whatever you wanted without a thought for tomorrow,
and now you have no money for food?

37
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:05,860
Who on earth would sympathize
with you after hearing that?

38
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:09,420
Even a broad-minded chief like him

39
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,440
would never do that!

40
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:14,120
If you want to eat plain
white rice every day,

41
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:17,740
how many times do I have to tell
you to plan how you spend your salary?

42
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:25,020
Make sure you engrave that feeling
of hunger deep into your stomach.

43
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:27,960
Got it? Say it:
"I will never waste money again."

44
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:29,780
Say it out loud.

45
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:33,800
Don't you forget those words.

46
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:37,300
Whatever you do,
don't give Ryotsu any money or valuables.

47
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,624
For someone who won't understand when told,

48
00:03:39,674 --> 00:03:41,900
the only option is to make
him learn it the hard way.

49
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:42,480
Yes!

50
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:48,420
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

51
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:52,140
Ryo-chan, wake up, Ryo-chan.

52
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:56,180
Let's deliver the package, come on.

53
00:03:57,280 --> 00:04:00,080
Ryo-chan,
I need your signature for this delivery.

54
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:02,740
Thanks for your business.

55
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,340
Rice!

56
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:12,206
Yahoo! It's rice, rice,

57
00:04:12,256 --> 00:04:13,480
I'm so happy!

58
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:15,460
That's a lot of hard work, isn't it?

59
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:17,860
What's this? This rice?

60
00:04:20,420 --> 00:04:21,260
It's mine, you know.

61
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:23,820
Look, senpai.

62
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:25,920
The other day,
at the supermarket in front of the station,

63
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,960
in the quiz for the
10th anniversary present,

64
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:29,440
you entered, remember?

65
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:32,640
So that's the prize from back then.

66
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:36,040
Heaven hasn't abandoned me after all.

67
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:37,860
This way I won't have to go without gas.

68
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:40,320
That's great, senpai.

69
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:42,500
What a man of incredible bad luck.

70
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:45,300
This rice is mine, you know.

71
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:47,220
If you touch it, you'll pay for this.

72
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:54,400
Mr. Smorzmo! Your order!

73
00:04:54,940 --> 00:04:56,780
I've brought the rice cooker!

74
00:04:57,460 --> 00:04:59,000
Yes! Here it comes, here it comes!

75
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:01,240
What's going on? Hey.

76
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:03,504
No, from the kitchen of Nikoniko Dormitory,

77
00:05:03,554 --> 00:05:05,820
I just borrowed it for a bit, that's all.

78
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:15,320
Ryo-chan, let me do it for you!

79
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:17,240
Don't you dare get in the way!

80
00:05:21,980 --> 00:05:25,140
He seems pretty worked up, so you'd
better stay away from him for a while.

81
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:53,420
He's like a wild beast!

82
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:56,660
Eating that fast,
your stomach won't be able to take it.

83
00:05:56,660 --> 00:06:00,940
See? I told you.

84
00:06:00,940 --> 00:06:02,960
Should I bring a washbasin?

85
00:06:12,460 --> 00:06:14,680
Wow, you ate it all!

86
00:06:15,180 --> 00:06:15,700
Well, then.

87
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:16,640
Um...

88
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:22,720
Are you going to eat more?

89
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:26,560
Itadakimasu!

90
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:34,400
Don't you get sick of just plain white rice?

91
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:43,140
Looks like you're getting
tired of it after all

92
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:45,760
Mm.

93
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:46,360
Mm.

94
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:47,880
Mm.

95
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:48,600
Mm.

96
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:48,940
Mm.

97
00:06:48,940 --> 00:06:49,220
Mm.

98
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:49,820
Mm.

99
00:06:49,820 --> 00:06:50,280
Mm.

100
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,220
Mm.

101
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:51,360
Mm.

102
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:51,560
Mm.

103
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:51,880
Mm.

104
00:06:51,880 --> 00:07:16,040
Mmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm

105
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:19,500
This fried rice-style rice,
seasoned with only salt and pepper,

106
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:23,400
doesn't mask the flavor of the rice itself,

107
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:26,740
and this stir-frying method, crisp on
the outside and fluffy on the inside,

108
00:07:26,740 --> 00:07:30,120
succeeds in bringing out the
texture of the rice to the fullest.

109
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:34,680
And there's the omurice-style fried rice,
seasoned with nothing but ketchup.

110
00:07:35,180 --> 00:07:37,400
The ketchup moistly coats the rice,

111
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:40,040
the ketchup wrapping up
the taste of the rice itself,

112
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:43,160
producing a rich, indescribable flavor.

113
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:48,100
And then there's the rice sushi,
enjoying fresh white rice as vinegared rice.

114
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:55,800
The natural taste of the rice and the vinegared rice never clash,
blending pleasantly on the tongue to create an exquisite harmony.

115
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:58,920
Well then, let's dig in!

116
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:03,060
Delicious!

117
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:07,460
Delicious!

118
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:12,760
This one's delicious too!

119
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:16,020
So good! It's too good!

120
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:19,920
Super delicious! Ultra delicious!

121
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:26,994
You two, you've been doing
nothing on the job this whole time,

122
00:08:27,044 --> 00:08:29,440
just sitting there watching me.

123
00:08:30,460 --> 00:08:32,750
Don't deny it, you two,

124
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:34,620
you want this food too, don't you?

125
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:39,506
You gave me such a cold shoulder earlier,

126
00:08:39,556 --> 00:08:41,260
like I'd ever share with you!

127
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:45,000
But I'm not a monster, you know.

128
00:08:45,620 --> 00:08:48,100
Honda's fine, but the other two,

129
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:49,086
Ryotsu-sama,

130
00:08:49,136 --> 00:08:52,720
please say you're deeply sorry for earlier.

131
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:56,980
If you just kneel and grovel,
I might let you have some.

132
00:08:58,440 --> 00:09:01,340
Why should I have to apologize?!

133
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:03,380
That's right, I'll never apologize!

134
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:04,900
Really? Fine, then.

135
00:09:04,900 --> 00:09:06,220
Then fiiiine!

136
00:09:08,220 --> 00:09:09,400
So delicious!

137
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:12,364
Honorable referee,

138
00:09:12,414 --> 00:09:16,260
I sincerely apologize for earlier.

139
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:18,635
the world of rice is

140
00:09:18,685 --> 00:09:21,160
endlessly vast!

141
00:09:22,780 --> 00:09:24,100
Sorry to keep you waiting.

142
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:28,200
Voilà, inside is fried rice on rice.

143
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:31,480
Plain fried rice with rice on the side!

144
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:33,820
This is truly the ultimate dish.

145
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:38,560
And for Reiko, a healthy okayu rice,

146
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:41,960
wait, isn't this okayu poured over rice?

147
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:43,700
It's bukkake meshi, isn't it?

148
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:47,140
This is truly the ultimate dish!

149
00:09:47,660 --> 00:09:50,300
And for Honda, a special zaru rice.

150
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:52,040
Zaru rice.

151
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:55,820
Slurp it down smoothly, like zaru soba.

152
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:56,760
Slurp, slurp.

153
00:09:58,840 --> 00:09:59,800
Itadakimasu!

154
00:10:02,660 --> 00:10:05,860
This is the ultimate dish, how about it?

155
00:10:05,860 --> 00:10:08,280
It's an indescribable flavor.

156
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:10,540
As expected, it just tastes like rice.

157
00:10:10,540 --> 00:10:13,360
Senpai, this is hard to eat.

158
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:17,740
Eat every last grain.
We have to treasure rice.

159
00:10:17,740 --> 00:10:18,660
Ryo-san.

160
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:20,060
What?

161
00:10:26,100 --> 00:10:26,420
Please.

162
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:32,700
It's rice, isn't it.

163
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:33,660
Rice again.

164
00:10:33,660 --> 00:10:35,120
This is hard to eat.

165
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:37,700
What on earth is this?

166
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:40,120
The Let's Eat Rice Association.

167
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:41,980
What's that?

168
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:45,220
Ryo-chan,
when did you join a group like that?

169
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:46,520
This is hard to eat.

170
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:51,280
That campaign to come up
with a new name for rice,

171
00:10:51,280 --> 00:10:52,420
you sent in a postcard for.

172
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:55,266
So Komecchau,
the rice name I came up with, won a prize,

173
00:10:55,316 --> 00:10:57,160
and they sent it to you as the prize!

174
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:58,040
Komecchau-na?

175
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,260
That's the winner?

176
00:10:59,420 --> 00:10:59,540
Yes.

177
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:01,120
Komecchau is hard to eat!

178
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:05,440
But senpai,
what are you going to do with all this rice?

179
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:23,260
Ryo-chan, welcome!

180
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:24,640
Yo, auntie.

181
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:25,960
Nice to meet you.

182
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:28,440
This is one of my regular shops.

183
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:29,640
Is that so?

184
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:33,480
Auntie, like I said on the phone, I'm
going to borrow the storefront for a bit.

185
00:11:34,020 --> 00:11:36,420
Use whatever part you like.

186
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:38,340
Anyway, business is slow here, so.

187
00:11:44,660 --> 00:11:47,820
Got it!
This shop is so plain, it was hard to find!

188
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:50,160
We searched for ages.

189
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:51,440
I've been waiting.

190
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:53,199
But,

191
00:11:53,249 --> 00:11:57,440
Will this place really make money? It doesn't
look like there's any foot traffic at all.

192
00:11:58,200 --> 00:12:00,640
No need to worry. Here, look.

193
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:02,680
There are a lot of numbers here.

194
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:04,360
What are these numbers?

195
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:05,437
These are

196
00:12:05,487 --> 00:12:12,080
the hourly foot traffic data for the Kameari neighborhood
that I painstakingly worked out between patrols.

197
00:12:12,420 --> 00:12:14,320
Working that out during patrols, no less.

198
00:12:14,660 --> 00:12:16,500
I figured the day would
come when it'd come in handy.

199
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:18,998
With that kind of secret backing behind it,

200
00:12:19,048 --> 00:12:21,480
So I judged this to be the ideal spot.

201
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:24,075
Especially around here,
it's far from the station,

202
00:12:24,125 --> 00:12:27,200
and though there are plenty of factories,
there are extremely few places to eat.

203
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:30,730
With no convenience stores either, if you
want to talk about business opportunities,

204
00:12:30,780 --> 00:12:33,860
there's only the hamburger
shop across the street.

205
00:12:34,940 --> 00:12:36,168
Back in the day, at lunchtime,

206
00:12:36,218 --> 00:12:40,340
factory workers would come to our place to buy bread,
you know.

207
00:12:40,340 --> 00:12:44,640
A few years ago, construction
suddenly started across the street,

208
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:48,160
and then a voice said,
"We'll be rivals from now on, so take care of us."

209
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:53,200
Sorry, but this world is
survival of the fittest.

210
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:58,720
Since then,
foot traffic has dried up completely.

211
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:02,400
If that's the case,
I can run my business without any worries.

212
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:05,920
How about you take 30%
of the profits, ma'am?

213
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:09,100
Is that really all right?

214
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:10,860
Stall rent.

215
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:13,120
It's free to begin with, anyway.

216
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:16,040
That's right.
Besides, we don't even know if it'll sell.

217
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:17,940
It'll sell! Of course it'll sell.

218
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:20,420
Yes! It'll definitely sell!
No, I'll make it sell!

219
00:13:22,020 --> 00:13:23,920
You're going to sell these rice balls?

220
00:13:24,820 --> 00:13:27,680
Eating burgers every
day would get old, right?

221
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:30,720
And if you're Japanese,
you'd naturally start craving rice.

222
00:13:31,140 --> 00:13:31,500
I see.

223
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:33,160
As expected of Ryo-sama.

224
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:36,400
It's time.

225
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:39,040
What's this siren?

226
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:41,340
The lunch break signal.

227
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:49,540
How did so many customers
show up all of a sudden?

228
00:13:49,540 --> 00:13:51,660
Well, we can't let them beat us, either!

229
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:52,840
Battle start!

230
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:57,000
Come on in, come on in, welcome!

231
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,660
This is Ryotsu's Rice Ball Shop!

232
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:02,780
Today, to celebrate our grand opening,
we're having a special sale!

233
00:14:02,780 --> 00:14:05,640
Any one you like, just 50 yen each!

234
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:08,780
Salmon, cod roe, pickled plum,
kelp, any of them, 50 yen!

235
00:14:10,340 --> 00:14:11,480
Welcome! Welcome!

236
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:13,920
Fifty yen?! That's a steal, hey!

237
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:15,840
I'll have umeboshi and tarako!

238
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:17,500
Then I'll take tarako and a combo!

239
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:19,360
That'll be 350 yen!

240
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:21,940
Yeah, one salmon mayo and three combos.

241
00:14:22,340 --> 00:14:23,420
Yes, thank you for your business!

242
00:14:24,180 --> 00:14:26,800
Don't push, don't push! Line up single file!

243
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:27,880
What's going on?

244
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:31,180
The candy shop across the
way started selling rice balls,

245
00:14:31,230 --> 00:14:32,580
and all the customers went over there!

246
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:33,760
What?!

247
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:35,460
What should we do?!

248
00:14:37,780 --> 00:14:40,420
Senpai,
we've sold out of all 50 salmon rice balls!

249
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:43,160
The kelp and cod roe ones are sold out too.

250
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:44,940
We've got plenty of rice.

251
00:14:45,340 --> 00:14:46,720
They're wolfing down the rice nonstop.

252
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:47,660
Coming!

253
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:50,480
Already sold out?

254
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:53,500
The next batch will be ready shortly,
so please wait a moment.

255
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:56,720
Our hot and spicy Texas Burger is

256
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:59,700
We never keep our customers waiting,
no matter what.

257
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:01,560
Come on, right this way!

258
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:02,420
If you're going to be afraid,

259
00:15:02,420 --> 00:15:03,260
Yes, yes, yes.

260
00:15:08,020 --> 00:15:10,880
Aaaaaah!

261
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:31,780
If they're going Western,
we'll go all-out traditional Japanese.

262
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:36,820
I've got three rice cookers ready so we
don't run out halfway through like yesterday.

263
00:15:36,820 --> 00:15:42,700
And this is the taiyaki-shaped rice ball machine I developed,
which makes twenty onigiri at once!

264
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:45,880
I see, with this we can make them easily.

265
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:48,680
And anyone can make them the same size.

266
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:53,640
Look, Maria,
you can't pack the rice this tightly!

267
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:55,420
Why not, Ryo-sama?

268
00:15:55,420 --> 00:16:01,120
Even with the same amount of rice, if you
squeeze it this hard, it ends up this small.

269
00:16:01,540 --> 00:16:04,240
To make it look like more,
you have to make them loosely!

270
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:06,160
So it looks bigger, I see.

271
00:16:06,820 --> 00:16:10,760
Make more rice balls from one cup of rice.
That's what business is all about.

272
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:13,400
Basically,
each one is made with about 500 grains.

273
00:16:13,660 --> 00:16:16,700
How do I count out 500 grains?

274
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:18,980
Just put it on the scale
and you'll get a rough idea.

275
00:16:19,420 --> 00:16:22,840
This is about 480 grains. Add another 20.

276
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:23,520
Yes.

277
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:27,740
Hey, you put in too much.
That's 20 grains over.

278
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:29,700
Sorry, Ryo-san.

279
00:16:29,940 --> 00:16:32,740
You're a careless guy,
which is why you always overdo it.

280
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:34,620
Trouble, Ryo-san!

281
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:37,880
The hamburger shop across the street
has started selling rice balls!

282
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:38,980
What?!

283
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:43,700
Welcome, welcome!

284
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:46,680
Texas Burger has started
selling rice balls too!

285
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:50,040
And at 99 yen,
it's cheaper than Ryotsu's rice balls!

286
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:57,380
Clever little tricks, you heartless bastard!

287
00:16:57,680 --> 00:17:00,980
They're cheaper,
so everyone's going over there!

288
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:03,620
Should we match them and sell cheaper too?

289
00:17:04,620 --> 00:17:11,780
Falling for the enemy's bait and rushing into a price war is dangerous.
We keep our prices the same and raise the quality of our products instead.

290
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:20,680
Ahhh! Come on, come on! Choose your onigiri filling right here,
exactly how you like it -

291
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:25,080
Only at Ryotsu Onigiri Honpo,
with over 2,000 combinations!

292
00:17:25,800 --> 00:17:26,120
Me

293
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:28,620
Welcome!

294
00:17:28,980 --> 00:17:29,860
Good morning!

295
00:17:29,860 --> 00:17:31,260
Please, take a seat.

296
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:34,420
We'll offer combinations too!

297
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:35,620
Manager!

298
00:17:35,620 --> 00:17:40,320
Cheap, tasty, with 3,000 filling combinations:
how about a Texas Burger onigiri?

299
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:42,740
Cactus, pilea, lizard, and scorpion!

300
00:17:42,740 --> 00:17:45,020
Onigiri fillings you can only taste here.

301
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:45,640
Coming!

302
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:49,240
They're copying us again.

303
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:51,200
I've already thought of my next move.

304
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:53,300
Come on, above all, characters!

305
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:57,320
How about rice balls shaped like cute
animals or nostalgic anime characters?

306
00:17:57,320 --> 00:18:02,060
We can't lose to that kiddie gimmick.

307
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:03,460
Hey, Boss!

308
00:18:03,460 --> 00:18:06,080
Texas Burger's original adult onigiri!

309
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:08,260
Hey, Boss!

310
00:18:08,260 --> 00:18:10,740
This is the onigiri made for grown-ups.

311
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:14,360
And these are color onigiri.

312
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:18,980
They're all dyed with coffee, food coloring,
and other natural coloring, so they're safe.

313
00:18:20,080 --> 00:18:22,340
But the blue rice balls are a little creepy.

314
00:18:23,300 --> 00:18:24,700
They're colorful rice balls.

315
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:26,800
No matter how you look at it,

316
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:28,460
they look unappetizing.

317
00:18:28,460 --> 00:18:31,180
Then they're covered all
over with sushi toppings.

318
00:18:31,180 --> 00:18:31,980
Nigirimusubi.

319
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:34,620
And tekkamusubi wrapped in tuna.

320
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:36,520
They look hard to eat.

321
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:39,500
And then, the ultimate rice ball,

322
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:40,060
this one!

323
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:42,400
The world's three great delicacies: truffle,

324
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:43,480
foie gras, caviar,

325
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:45,260
matsutake, kazunoko, and so on.

326
00:18:45,260 --> 00:18:47,560
Packed with ultra-luxurious ingredients.

327
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:50,640
And instead of nori,
it's wrapped in gold leaf.

328
00:18:51,020 --> 00:18:52,420
An ultra-premium rice ball.

329
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:53,920
It's 5,000 yen!

330
00:18:54,260 --> 00:18:55,440
Will these actually sell?

331
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:59,340
Well, this is a special version for
parties and other occasions to draw a crowd.

332
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:00,080
I see.

333
00:19:01,860 --> 00:19:03,980
My ideas are endless!

334
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:06,160
How far can you keep up?

335
00:19:07,860 --> 00:19:11,620
Lottery onigiri, where one in ten wins gold,
silver, or diamond!

336
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:14,340
W-wait, please stop, shopkeeper!

337
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:16,880
If you do that, we'll go bankrupt!

338
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:22,840
Ryotsu Onigiri Honpo kept attracting more and
more customers with his endless stream of ideas.

339
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:29,740
With Nakagawa's help, he developed a vending machine
that grills frozen onigiri in ten seconds, a huge hit.

340
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:35,720
Under the slogan
"Make it yourself, since you're traveling," he sold handmade onigiri kits at station kiosks,

341
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:40,180
and vacuum-packed onigiri that
keep for 60 days were also big hits.

342
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:45,200
Ryotsu Onigiri Honpo was also featured
in the media and kept up steady sales.

343
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:46,400
Meanwhile,

344
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:52,920
They've really been trying all sorts of things,
haven't they.

345
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:55,220
I can't make out what that sound is at all.

346
00:19:55,220 --> 00:19:59,080
It's like watching the fate of that
coffee specialty shop by the bus stop.

347
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:02,760
Even with such a wide
variety of products on offer,

348
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:04,360
why aren't any customers coming?

349
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:04,811
Manager,

350
00:20:04,861 --> 00:20:09,880
I think we should go back to
the original burger shop, though.

351
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:12,900
Ryo-sama! Are you saying I'm mistaken?

352
00:20:14,780 --> 00:20:15,800
Tch, I hate this.

353
00:20:16,540 --> 00:20:17,760
Traitors get fired!

354
00:20:19,700 --> 00:20:20,020
And then

355
00:20:20,020 --> 00:20:20,500
And then...

356
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:23,280
Ryo-sama! The burger shop across the street!

357
00:20:23,540 --> 00:20:24,780
So it finally went under!

358
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:32,360
It's becoming an even
more incomprehensible shop.

359
00:20:32,740 --> 00:20:34,820
It's completely lost its way.

360
00:20:35,980 --> 00:20:37,160
Condolences.

361
00:20:38,860 --> 00:20:41,745
Afterward, the hamburger shop kept changing,
first into a video rental store,

362
00:20:41,795 --> 00:20:44,120
then a Famicom shop, and so on...

363
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:48,300
Looks like it's settled
into a monthly parking lot

364
00:20:50,020 --> 00:20:58,600
Steady is best, you know. Not that it's always a sure bet!
Booms are just temporary, after all.
They'll get tired of it soon enough.

365
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:07,280
So Ryotsu Onigiri Honpo is going to make a big gamble
with the whole world in its sights. I've got a bad feeling about this.

366
00:21:15,140 --> 00:21:16,400
They're really going all out, aren't they.

367
00:21:16,920 --> 00:21:19,340
Senpai, get Kome-cchau-na as a sponsor.

368
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:21,300
and invite the foreign media too.

369
00:21:21,620 --> 00:21:25,480
I heard you said Ryotsu Onigiri
Honpo is launching a huge campaign...

370
00:21:38,180 --> 00:21:38,820
It's done!

371
00:21:38,820 --> 00:21:40,260
Making the Guinness Book is a sure thing.

372
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:44,120
This is Japan's traditional fast food.

373
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:45,340
It's an onigiri.

374
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:48,320
Ryotsu Onigiri Honpo is right now

375
00:21:48,320 --> 00:21:51,580
having completed the
world's biggest onigiri!

376
00:21:51,580 --> 00:21:55,440
Alright, Boss,
would you mind riding on top of the onigiri?

377
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:56,660
Very well!

378
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:00,578
Alright, since we're at it,

379
00:22:00,628 --> 00:22:03,540
let's parade this onigiri around the
neighborhood like a portable shrine!

380
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:04,700
Ooh!

381
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:10,480
Wasshai! Wasshai! Wasshai!
Wasshai! Wasshai! Wasshai!

382
00:22:10,480 --> 00:22:11,219
Asōre,

383
00:22:11,269 --> 00:22:15,060
Wasshai! Wasshai! Wasshai! Wasshai!

384
00:22:15,060 --> 00:22:16,114
Asōre,

385
00:22:16,164 --> 00:22:20,140
Wasshai! Wasshai! Wasshai!

386
00:22:21,580 --> 00:22:29,440


387
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:32,080
Because of this, my life has
been completely thrown off course.

388
00:22:32,580 --> 00:22:35,060
Stripped down to nothing,
I've got to start over from scratch again.

389
00:22:39,220 --> 00:22:40,520
Somebody stop me!

390
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:48,180
Copycat

391
00:23:06,260 --> 00:23:08,980
No good! It'll spread to
the warehouse over there too!

392
00:23:16,060 --> 00:23:17,280
Help! Help!

393
00:23:20,260 --> 00:23:22,200
He really outdid himself this time,
didn't he.

394
00:23:22,760 --> 00:23:27,060
Thanks to that, they say the term
"yaki-onigiri" has become world-famous.

395
00:23:27,060 --> 00:23:27,382
But,

396
00:23:27,432 --> 00:23:31,900
the "Kome-chau" name will hurt the image,
so they're changing it, right?

397
00:23:32,340 --> 00:23:35,920
We were lucky to get out
of that fire alive senpai.

398
00:23:36,120 --> 00:23:37,900
Poor Ryo-sama!

399
00:23:38,220 --> 00:23:39,610
Hmph, you big idiot.

400
00:23:39,660 --> 00:23:42,540
You wasted rice,
so you got what you deserved.

401
00:23:42,820 --> 00:23:46,120
Ryotsu's bills for everything
he broke are piling up like this.

402
00:23:46,220 --> 00:23:49,460
S-so, could it be,
could it possibly be that senpai...?

403
00:23:49,580 --> 00:23:52,920
He'll probably be working for free
and going without meals for a while.

404
00:23:57,060 --> 00:23:59,460
Ryotsu, we're gonna get rice-ruined!

405
00:24:27,100 --> 00:24:33,320
Acting all chic with a baguette in hand, but
it's a beef bowl with extra sauce, cloudy and all.

406
00:24:33,320 --> 00:24:40,300
Frustration from endless overtime,
cleared away neatly with more frustration.

407
00:24:43,660 --> 00:24:50,080
Every day's a no-problem blend,
once I've run through a hot shower.

408
00:24:50,080 --> 00:24:56,660
Every day's a no-problem brain,
energy restored with a sleep pillow.

409
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:06,280
Every day's a no-problem brain,
I love even someone like me.

410
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:13,100
Every day's a no-problem brain,
a Monday with hearts flying around.

411
00:25:13,100 --> 00:25:17,240
Perfect score, perfect score,
no-problem brain.

412
00:25:20,080 --> 00:25:21,980
Kicked out when the dorm was rebuilt, I

413
00:25:21,980 --> 00:25:24,220
ended up crashing at the Chief's house.

414
00:25:24,220 --> 00:25:26,300
And it's so cramped already.

415
00:25:26,300 --> 00:25:27,300
Everyone's tiptoeing around me.

416
00:25:27,300 --> 00:25:30,000
On top of that,
booze and gambling are all banned.

417
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:30,800
Damn it!

418
00:25:30,800 --> 00:25:33,440
I'll turn this around somehow!

419
00:25:33,940 --> 00:25:34,500
Next time

420
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:36,500
The hellish boarding life.

421
00:25:37,080 --> 00:25:37,660
Take care of me, won't you.

